WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.638
The authors make a simple observation.

00:00:02.718 --> 00:00:06.285
In a batch of unlabeled test images of one product,

00:00:06.365 --> 00:00:10.576
a normal patch finds many similar patches across
the others,

00:00:10.656 --> 00:00:13.007
because normal appearance repeats.

00:00:13.087 --> 00:00:17.227
An abnormal patch finds only a few, since defects
are rare.

00:00:17.307 --> 00:00:21.160
That asymmetry is a signal already inside the test set.
